1
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:45,530
Do you like the dress?

2
00:00:45,530 --> 00:00:46,530
I love it.

3
00:00:46,530 --> 00:00:48,530
I designed it myself.

4
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:49,530
It's beautiful.

5
00:00:49,530 --> 00:00:51,530
Are you ready?

6
00:00:51,530 --> 00:00:53,530
We're supposed to be there

7
00:00:53,530 --> 00:00:54,530
before the guests arrive.

8
00:00:54,530 --> 00:00:55,530
I know. I know.

9
00:00:55,530 --> 00:01:02,530
Help me with this tie, will you?

10
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:04,530
Honey, I'm scared to death.

11
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:09,530
But this is what you've been working for all these years.

12
00:01:09,530 --> 00:01:10,530
No, no.

13
00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:12,530
I worked to put together a book of photographs.

14
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:13,530
This is show business.

15
00:01:13,530 --> 00:01:15,530
Well, it's all part of the same job.

16
00:01:15,530 --> 00:01:17,530
Just relax and enjoy it.

17
00:01:17,530 --> 00:01:20,530
You're right.

18
00:01:20,530 --> 00:01:25,530
I earned this, and I'm going to enjoy it.

19
00:01:25,530 --> 00:01:31,530
As soon as I recover from my nervous breakdown.

20
00:01:31,530 --> 00:01:36,530
What are you afraid of?

21
00:01:36,530 --> 00:01:37,530
Everything.

22
00:01:37,530 --> 00:01:39,530
A critic was there this morning.

23
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:40,530
He probably hates my work.

24
00:01:40,530 --> 00:01:43,530
I have to sign copies of my book for a lot of people

25
00:01:43,530 --> 00:01:44,530
I never met before.

26
00:01:44,530 --> 00:01:46,530
My new shoes hurt my feet ...

27
00:01:46,530 --> 00:01:58,530
You're going to be a great success.

28
00:01:58,530 --> 00:02:02,530
Are you ready?

29
00:02:02,530 --> 00:02:04,530
As soon as I get these cuff links on.

30
00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:05,530
Let me help.

31
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:12,530
Mom and Dad are already on their way down to the gallery.

32
00:02:12,530 --> 00:02:20,530
There! You look very attractive.

33
00:02:20,530 --> 00:02:23,530
Thank you.

34
00:02:23,530 --> 00:02:26,530
Well, I suppose I've run out of excuses.

35
00:02:26,530 --> 00:02:29,530
Mm-hmm. Let's go ...

36
00:02:29,530 --> 00:02:32,530
Oh, one minute.

37
00:02:32,530 --> 00:02:35,530
Before we go to the gallery,

38
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:37,530
I just want to tell you

39
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:38,530
that I never could have done this book

40
00:02:38,530 --> 00:02:40,530
without your help and your love.

41
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:43,530
I appreciate it.

42
00:02:43,530 --> 00:02:45,530
Thanks.

43
00:02:45,530 --> 00:03:00,530
Now, no more stalling.

44
00:03:00,530 --> 00:03:01,530
What is it?

45
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:02,530
There's nobody here!

46
00:03:02,530 --> 00:03:05,530
Of course not, Richard.

47
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:08,530
Your show doesn't begin until eight thirty.

48
00:03:08,530 --> 00:03:12,530
Oh. Right.

49
00:03:12,530 --> 00:03:16,530
Richard! Welcome! Good luck tonight! Richard

50
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:17,530
Well, thanks.

51
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:19,530
This is my publisher, Harvey Carlson.

52
00:03:19,530 --> 00:03:20,530
You've met my wife Marilyn ...

53
00:03:20,530 --> 00:03:22,530
Charmed.

54
00:03:22,530 --> 00:03:24,530
My mother, Ellen Stewart.

55
00:03:24,530 --> 00:03:25,530
Harvey Carlson.

56
00:03:25,530 --> 00:03:26,530
It's good to meet you.

57
00:03:26,530 --> 00:03:29,530
This is my father, Dr. Philip Stewart ...

58
00:03:29,530 --> 00:03:30,530
Nice to meet you, Mr. Carlson.

59
00:03:30,530 --> 00:03:31,530
My brother Robbie ...

60
00:03:31,530 --> 00:03:32,530
Hi.

61
00:03:32,530 --> 00:03:33,530
Hi.

62
00:03:33,530 --> 00:03:36,530
And this is my sister Susan and her husband Harry Bennett

63
00:03:36,530 --> 00:03:37,530
and his daughter Michelle.

64
00:03:37,530 --> 00:03:39,530
It's nice to meet you.

65
00:03:39,530 --> 00:03:43,530
And this gentleman is my grandfather, Malcolm Stewart.

66
00:03:43,530 --> 00:03:45,530
Welcome, Mr. Stewart.

67
00:03:45,530 --> 00:03:48,530
Well, make yourselves comfortable.

68
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:51,530
There are hors d'oeuvres at the table, fruit punch at the bar.

69
00:03:51,530 --> 00:03:52,530
Help yourselves.

70
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:55,530
Can I get you something, Mr. Stewart?

71
00:03:55,530 --> 00:03:56,530
No, thank you.

72
00:03:56,530 --> 00:03:59,530
You can feel very proud of your grandson, Mr. Stewart.

73
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:01,530
I do.

74
00:04:01,530 --> 00:04:04,530
I'm proud of all my grandchildren, Mr. Carlson.

75
00:04:04,530 --> 00:04:05,530
Of course.

76
00:04:05,530 --> 00:04:06,530
Feel free to look around.

77
00:04:06,530 --> 00:04:08,530
If you need anything, just ask.

78
00:04:08,530 --> 00:04:09,530
Thank you.

79
00:04:09,530 --> 00:04:11,530
Harvey? Harvey

80
00:04:11,530 --> 00:04:12,530
Yes?

81
00:04:12,530 --> 00:04:14,530
Did Mitchell Johnson's review come out yet? Mitchell Johnsson

82
00:04:14,530 --> 00:04:15,530
Not yet.

83
00:04:15,530 --> 00:04:17,530
The newspapers don't come out till about ten o'clock.

84
00:04:17,530 --> 00:04:19,530
When they come out, we'll get it.

85
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:20,530
Thanks.

86
00:04:20,530 --> 00:04:22,530
Ready?

87
00:04:22,530 --> 00:04:25,530
Yes. Have the people arrived?

88
00:04:25,530 --> 00:04:26,530
The guests are waiting.

89
00:04:26,530 --> 00:04:28,530
Tom's about to open the doors. Tom

90
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:31,530
Good luck! And stop worrying!

91
00:04:31,530 --> 00:04:34,530
They're going to love it.
